,"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7036032","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"239b60c05927e24e43dc0b722463ae64983ff28469cffcec9d8aa069d0028813","compact":"5b8475e122b268569d1741826c9e00b61e247647e851f500ff5a2a02787cc861","nasal":"8c05f86ec062ba12ddc2c84423c67be4213712751eb658de54b641059a4289a8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-36-33","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":36,"verse":33,"english":"That you will be unconscious of the prowess endowed with which you torment us. You will be conscious of your power only after being reminded of it.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-36-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7036033","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"53f34289687d5e26be7e993bdda64697b8e585cd43e30ae2e9f7c049cdf98072","compact":"d2e34b4632df5f754bd4415cd10e5a15f2646396969f5f7332348b6dcd5b9f94","nasal":"d2e34b4632df5f754bd4415cd10e5a15f2646396969f5f7332348b6dcd5b9f94"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-36-34","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":36,"verse":34,"english":"Thereupon, having devoid of prowess and glory, he used to wander in the hermitages silently and decently.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.296,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-36-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7036034","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"04c94b2c322f6f85d3058b98560b722fdffedccafb4e32b3a22e5cf214ece06c","compact":"ff9cfc342eb569765b5f3084549fbf009391ce331dc12ee4ae25f3264b8c4940","nasal":"ff9cfc342eb569765b5f3084549fbf009391ce331dc12ee4ae25f3264b8c4940"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-36-35","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":36,"verse":35,"english":"There was a king of all Mongoloids named as Rkşarajā; the father of Vāli and Sugrīva. He was as glorious as the Sun.","alignment":{"typ