d an unbrokeable friendship with Sugrīva like air with the fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-36-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7036038","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3979ab6dbe1ca6bba2baf046678aa54e0898fdf219c86f9c1e3f66a3ed476559","compact":"4ac557b90bf0c7b962519fe06ca9e909be02bb9e18cb74ead85ce8e4cbd73e9a","nasal":"4ac557b90bf0c7b962519fe06ca9e909be02bb9e18cb74ead85ce8e4cbd73e9a"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-36-39","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":36,"verse":39,"english":"O Rāma! Hanuman could not be conscious of his power due to the curse at the time of altercations between Sugrīva and Vāli.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.673,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-36-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7036039","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6cbbaeac2a68b6213f905f48d670c11fddd752092d6008c8f6e6bd42e771264a","compact":"974658b3a42ed9a0b6eef3b3b7e62ead7d88082299fbfe218a4919077ad72014","nasal":"974658b3a42ed9a0b6eef3b3b7e62ead7d88082299fbfe218a4919077ad72014"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-36-40","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":36,"verse":40,"english":"In fact, O Rama! wondering Sugriva also did not know about the might of Hanumān.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.627,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-36-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7036040","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c276ef94ff6453f81b0c58f1e51866bcaa836ed4e628177a8f3a3e33a0a40a97","compact":"a1cb1e4046573ed3233dc0cf9c0bfec5170c1325bb400f72e5eb99c05921f85f","nasal":"a1cb1e4046573ed3233dc0cf9c0bfec5170c1325bb400f72e5eb99c05921f85f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-36-41","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":36,"verse":41,"english":"Who is there in the world superior to Hanumān in respect of prowess, enthusiasm, intelligence, glory, well behavedness, sweetness, diplomacy or otherwise profundity, shrewdness, virility and patience.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.34,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-36-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7036041","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"51dbf57787dc6d3a4db27fed4f11a795bf4f968f66ad34f4de4db21da04cf90b","compact":"ca77d373f0ddb96ae421087f9664dc45145af306027c9303c199a9de82c94b28","nasal":"43281714bdb8db8ca283e6e6314dc9d8083cddde5f6a80b73c7fafd727d7cc65"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-36-42","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":36,"verse":42,"english":"Having curiosity to learn grammar, the best of Mongols of immeasurable power went towards the hill of rising Sun facing Sunward with the view to ask queries and to master the great work.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.688,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-36-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7036042","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de58573825cebaf1affa77c781d858c8d8eb6be8ca9c7a4f8e455a6652bb60a7","compact":"943114af079fe6e871c13cb4b35e6a001e3c9f9c56f9f637491601fa5e684b2d","nasal":"4d1f58664c00d5393c33fd65057910461a264ee1445592d9c4c792fc6213d029"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-36-43","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":36,"verse":43,"english":"He actually rivals the teacher of gods, i.e. Bșhaspati in all the branches of learning and austerities. Who can stand before Hanuman who resembled like ocean likely to engulf the worlds and like fire likely to burn the worlds at the time of decreation of universo.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-36-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7036043","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 18